### Manual requests against the running API (`dotnet run --project src/IdleHold.Api`).
### In VS Code, install the "REST Client" extension and click "Send Request" above each block.

@host = http://localhost:5085

### List game content
GET {{host}}/content

### Create a player (copy the "id" from the response into @playerId below)
POST {{host}}/players

###
@playerId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Get player state (caught up to now)
GET {{host}}/players/{{playerId}}

### Start chopping pine
POST {{host}}/players/{{playerId}}/action
Content-Type: application/json

{ "actionId": "cut-pine" }

### Craft the chipped stone axe (needs 3 twigs and 2 pebbles; 409 without them or once you own it)
POST {{host}}/players/{{playerId}}/action
Content-Type: application/json

{ "actionId": "craft-chipped-stone-axe" }

### Stop the current action
DELETE {{host}}/players/{{playerId}}/action
